"""扩展装备表：新增福利补偿设备与专业装备条目。

在 ii（装备说明页）数组尾部追加新条目，并保持原数组结构不变。
"""

# 追加到 ii 数组末尾的装备条目（不含最外层 [] 包裹）
GEAR_ITEMS = r'''
,{id:"emergency-kit",name:()=>i("应急装备包","Emergency kit"),what:()=>i("一个塞满应急物品的包：备用气瓶、保温毯、能量胶、一小卷胶带。","A bag of emergency gear: a spare cylinder, a thermal blanket, energy gel, a roll of tape."),when:()=>i("每一次都带。洞里的东西，永远是缺的。","Every dive. Whatever the cave lacks, you bring it."),why:()=>i("福利补偿设备说的就是这个：出事的概率不大，但一旦出事，缺一样东西就是致命的。应急装备不增加你的能力，它只决定出事以后你能不能回家。","This is what a welfare-support kit means: the odds of something going wrong are low, but if it does happen, one missing item is the difference between coming back and not. Emergency kit does not make you more capable; it decides whether you come home.")}
,{id:"thermal-blanket",name:()=>i("保温毯","Thermal blanket"),what:()=>i("一张能折叠成钱包大小的铝箔毯。","A foil blanket that folds into the size of a wallet."),when:()=>i("带人出水之后，或者自己冷得发抖的时候。","After bringing someone out, or when you are shaking with cold."),why:()=>i("洞里的水常年四度，人在冷水里泡半小时，体温掉得比你想的快。保温毯裹上，体温回升比干衣快得多。","Cave water sits at four degrees; half an hour in it drops your core temperature faster than you would guess. Wrapped in foil, you rewarm far faster than in a drysuit.")}
,{id:"spare-cylinder",name:()=>i("应急备用气瓶","Emergency cylinder"),what:()=>i("一支 3 升的小瓶，挂在腰上或者放进包里。","A 3-litre cylinder on your waist or in the bag."),when:()=>i("给没气的人分气，或者给自己留最后一口气。","To share with someone out of gas, or to keep for your own last breath."),why:()=>i("三分之一的第三份不是用来潜得更远的，是用来出事的。一支小瓶在最坏的时候，能让两个人多在水里待几分钟。","The last third of the plan is not for going deeper; it is for the emergency. A small cylinder can buy two people a few more minutes when everything has gone wrong.")}
,{id:"stove-warm",name:()=>i("应急热源","Heat source"),what:()=>i("一枚化学发热片，捏两下就热。","A chemical heat pack that warms when you crack it."),when:()=>i("上岸之后，队友失温发抖的时候。","On the bank, when a teammate is hypothermic and shaking."),why:()=>i("冷水里的失温，核心是先暖躯干，不是先暖手脚。发热片贴着胸腹，比喝热水管用。","In cold-water exposure the core goes first, not the extremities. A heat pack against the chest and belly does more than a hot drink.")}
,{id:"camera-kit",name:()=>i("水下相机","Underwater camera"),what:()=>i("一台装在防水壳里的相机，两只闪光灯，一只腕灯。","A camera in a housing, two strobes, a wrist light."),when:()=>i("有拍摄任务的时候。","When there is a photography assignment."),why:()=>i("洞潜摄影不是为了好看，是为了记录：哪道缝、哪个洞室、哪条支洞。照片回到岸上才是资料，水下看谁都一样黑。","Cave photography is not for pretty pictures; it is for the record: which restriction, which chamber, which side passage. The photos only become data once they are on land, because underwater everything is the same black.")}
,{id:"water-sampler",name:()=>i("水质取样瓶","Water sampler"),what:()=>i("三只 100 毫升的取样瓶，带编号。","Three 100 ml sample bottles, numbered."),when:()=>i("水质考察任务：在指定深度的取样点各取一瓶。","Water-quality assignments: one bottle at each sampling point."),why:()=>i("水的温度、酸碱度、浊度、溶解氧，各在不同深度取样才有意义。同一层的取样点之间也要隔开距离，别让上一瓶的水影响下一瓶。","Temperature, pH, turbidity and dissolved oxygen only mean something when sampled at different depths. Keep the sampling points apart too, so one bottle does not contaminate the next.")}
,{id:"slate-kit",name:()=>i("测绘与采样记录板","Survey and sampling slate"),what:()=>i("一块水下写字板，刻度、深度、编号都能记。","A writable underwater slate for depth, bearing and sample numbers."),when:()=>i("任何一次带任务的潜。","On any dive with an assignment."),why:()=>i("水下只记数字：站号、深度、方位、样本编号。图是回到岸上才画的，画出来才发现数据缺了，就是白潜一趟。","Underwater you only write numbers: station, depth, bearing, sample number. The map is drawn on land, and if a number is missing then, the dive was wasted.")}
,{id:"rebreather-oxygen",name:()=>i("闭路供氧备件","Rebreather oxygen spares"),what:()=>i("一组电控电池、一包备用洗涤剂、一个手动加氧器。","A set of controller cells, a spare scrubber pack and a manual add-oxygen valve."),when:()=>i("背循环呼吸器的时候。","Whenever you dive a rebreather."),why:()=>i("闭路潜水最怕的是安静地出事：洗涤剂耗尽，供氧失灵，没有预兆。备件不是配件，是装备能不能继续工作的前提。","The rebreather's worst failure is the quiet one: a spent scrubber, a dead oxygen cell, no warning. The spares are not accessories; they are the condition of the equipment still working.")}
,{id:"lift-bag-spare",name:()=>i("备用浮力袋","Spare lift bag"),what:()=>i("一只小一号的浮力袋，卷起来塞在包里。","A smaller lift bag, rolled into the bag."),when:()=>i("带遗体或者重物出水的时候。","When bringing a casualty or heavy gear up."),why:()=>i("一只袋子不够用，是最常见的计划外情况。备用浮力袋能把「只能丢下」变成「两趟」——多跑一趟，比少一样东西强。","The most common unplanned problem is one bag not being enough. A spare turns \"we have to leave it\" into \"we make two trips\": an extra round beats going without.")}
'''

